1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,010
The equation said both sides must move together. Debit and credit are only the
two sides of that one line. Neither word means good or bad.

2
00:00:10,030 --> 00:00:14,546
A debit is the left side of an account. A
credit is the right side.

3
00:00:14,566 --> 00:00:20,090
Every journal entry needs at least one of
each, and the totals must match.

4
00:00:20,110 --> 00:00:23,696
Buying supplies with cash increases an
asset on the left and decreases another
asset on the right. Debit supplies.

5
00:00:23,716 --> 00:00:27,903
Credit cash.

6
00:00:27,923 --> 00:00:32,110
The line still balances.

7
00:00:32,130 --> 00:00:36,826
Do not memorise “debit means increase.

8
00:00:36,846 --> 00:00:42,328
” Name the account on the left and the
account on the right, then check the
amounts.

9
00:00:42,348 --> 00:00:47,830
Next we ask when that line is dated — when
cash moves, or when the work is done.

